### Accessibility Features

#### Automatic Accessibility
- **Base UI handles ARIA attributes** automatically
- **Custom form components** inherit Base UI accessibility
- **Keyboard navigation** built into all interactive components
- **Screen reader support** for all components
- **Focus management** handled by components

#### Custom Accessibility
```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Maintain accessibility when customizing
const CustomSelect = () => (
    <ValidatedCustomSelect
        field="class"
        label="Choose character class"
        options={classOptions}
        labelExtraClassName="sr-only" // Screen reader only label
    />
);
```

### Success Criteria
- [ ] Custom form components used for all form controls
- [ ] Form validation integrated properly
- [ ] Consistent Tailwind CSS styling applied
- [ ] Accessibility features maintained
- [ ] Component composition follows patterns
- [ ] Keyboard navigation works correctly
- [ ] Screen reader compatibility verified

**CRITICAL**: Always prefer custom form components from `@forms/` over base Base UI components for form controls.
